"""Seed the info pages' strings (website redesign step 3, group "info"): /about, /about/sources, /quality-standards,
/process/11-step-filtration (unit "info-company"); /contact, /coverage and /gallery (unit "info-contact").

Follows the pattern of scripts/seed_web_ui_shell_translations.py:
- keys under `web.info.*`, en / ru / uz for every key; Uzbek Latin with ‘ in o‘/g‘ and ’ for the tutuq belgisi (never
  ʻ U+02BB, which Manrope lacks, and never a straight ');
- /about/sources and the filtration page kept their copy in Jinja dicts inside the templates; it moved here word for
  word (the citation wording is what LLMs quote), except: the `**label**:` Markdown became a label key and a text key;
  the support address became `{email}` (the page prints MAIL_SUPPORT_EMAIL as a mailto link); the sources page no
  longer claims a regulator link it never showed, and the JSON feed is "on this page", not "below";
- the mineral table and the regulator sentence were typed twice per language (six copies): one set of keys now serves
  both pages;
- /contact lost its form (it posted to an API route that never existed): the channels and hours are keys here, the
  links come from config; /coverage's FAQ is printed on the page and repeated by its FAQPage JSON-LD from the same
  keys (the English answers are the old JSON-LD wording, word for word);
- customer copy never tells the customer to phone, states only facts backed by /about/sources, the filtration page or
  the Product rows (prices and sizes are printed live from the offer facts, never typed here);
- `Translation.bulk_create_or_update` inserts the missing rows, updates only the keys listed here and drops their
  Redis cache entries, so a re-run is safe. Never drop a key another unit of the group added.

Run on the dev database (scripts/ is not mounted in the container, so pipe it in):
    docker compose exec -T business_app python - < scripts/seed_web_ui_info_translations.py
"""

